rness code — and must be NOCOW (`chattr +C`): cargo-mutants 27.1.0 copies the tree (`target/` included, ~14 GB) into `std::env::temp_dir()`, `/tmp` there is a 32 GB `usrquota` tmpfs (a full viola-e2e run died at 460/709 on `Disk quota exceeded`), and on a COW btrfs dir its reflink copy drops the exec bit of the prebuilt `viola-fake-agent` (as measured at `viola-0.1.0/chunks/2026-10-03-mutation-scoring-completion/evidence/m3.md`); a NOCOW dir makes the reflink fail over to the mode-keeping `fs::copy`. No document prints this path either.
